# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify rewrite rules for the Eilatush PWA
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is auto-detected by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages (they share
# the same `_redirects` format).  It serves three purposes:
#
#  1. Map clean URLs to their static HTML files (e.g. /sources → /sources.html)
#  2. Provide an SPA fallback for dynamic routes (e.g. /business/abc123)
#  3. Ensure the service worker is never proxied through a cache
#
# Order matters — more specific rules come first.

# ── 1) Asset shortcuts (no rewrite, just cache hints) ────────────────────
# (Handled by `_headers` file below)

# ── 2) Dynamic routes: /business/:id, /article/:id, /job/:id ─────────────
# Expo Router exports a generic [id].html for each, so map any sub-path
# to the corresponding template.  This is essentially an SPA fallback.
/business/*    /business/[id].html    200
/article/*     /article/[id].html     200
/job/*         /job/[id].html         200

# ── 3) Tab routes — Expo Router exports both /tab and /(tabs)/tab .html ───
/                   /index.html         200
/eilatush           /eilatush.html      200
/businesses         /businesses.html    200
/news               /news.html          200
/jobs               /jobs.html          200
/sources            /sources.html       200

# ── 4) Final SPA fallback — anything unknown serves index.html ───────────
# This lets client-side routing handle any unforeseen path.
/*                  /index.html         200
